# Shared build context for the api, web and worker images (all built from the repository root, see
# infra/docker-compose.yml). The api image has its own services/api/Dockerfile.dockerignore, which BuildKit
# prefers over this file for that build.

.git
.claude

# Dependency directories and caches are reinstalled inside the image; sending host copies only slows the build
# and can shadow the in-image install.
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.gradle
**/.kotlin
**/build
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# Local footage, datasets and model weights must never reach the daemon. The ml CLIs write datasets to data/ and
# models to a directory of the user's choice relative to where they run, which can be inside ml/, and the worker
# image copies ml/ wholesale, so these are matched at any depth rather than only at the root. The worker gets its
# trained model through MODEL_DIR at runtime, never from the image.
**/data
**/*.mp4
**/*.mov
**/*.mkv
**/*.m4v
**/*.pt
**/*.pth
**/*.onnx

# Local env files hold secrets. The worker and web images copy whole service directories, so a stray .env there
# would otherwise be baked into the image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# apps/client is the Kotlin Multiplatform app and no image needs it. apps/web is not excluded because
# apps/web/Dockerfile copies it from this same context.
apps/client
